# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability suppressions
# Generated by arbiter. Edit to add project-specific suppressions.
#
# POLICY — The following vulnerability categories MUST NOT be suppressed
# without a documented security exception approved by the security team:
#   SQL_INJECTION, XSS, COMMAND_INJECTION, LDAP_INJECTION, HARD_CODE_PASSWORD
#
# MANDATORY FORMAT (INV-31): every suppression entry MUST be a single line —
#   <CVE-ID> exp:<YYYY-MM-DD> # reason=<10+ chars, reference a tracking issue> owner=@<github-handle>
#
# The check-suppressions.mjs gate validates every entry on every L1 commit.
# Entries with a past exp: date fail the gate — there are no permanent
# suppressions. Entries missing reason/owner fail the gate too.
#
# Example:
# CVE-2023-XXXXX exp:2026-12-31 # reason=False positive, only affects containerized deployments (#1234) owner=@yourhandle

